WEBVTT

00:01.060 --> 00:03.020
Let's play the king game!

00:03.730 --> 00:06.060
<i>Near the end of summer break,</i>

00:06.400 --> 00:08.650
<i>Misuzu and Carol came to spend the night.</i>

00:09.400 --> 00:11.110
I'm the king.

00:11.110 --> 00:12.070
Huh?

00:12.070 --> 00:14.660
And what's your order?

00:14.660 --> 00:17.490
Tomo-chan has to do an 
impersonation of Misuzu-chan.

00:17.490 --> 00:20.330
What?! I can't impersonate Misuzu!

00:20.330 --> 00:21.700
Okay, then I will.

00:21.700 --> 00:22.410
Wait, why?!

00:23.960 --> 00:26.420
I'll slaughter you socially.

00:31.260 --> 00:33.130
I'm the king.

00:33.130 --> 00:34.720
Yikes! Misuzu?!

00:34.720 --> 00:36.300
I'm scared.

00:36.300 --> 00:40.680
Okay, Tomo... You will go to the 
fireworks show with Junichiro.

00:40.680 --> 00:41.350
Huh?

00:42.350 --> 00:46.020
King

00:42.980 --> 00:45.350
Just the two of you this time.

00:56.740 --> 01:02.040
<i>When I throw a jab or a straight,
 it always lands</i>

01:02.040 --> 01:07.170
<i>But when I'm aiming for your heart,
 I miss every time</i>

01:07.170 --> 01:12.500
<i>Parallel, zigzagging, awkward, incoherent</i>

01:12.500 --> 01:17.010
<i>When you look my way and move closer to me</i>

01:17.010 --> 01:22.770
<i>I know it doesn't mean the same thing for you</i>

01:22.770 --> 01:27.810
<i>But I wish we could stay like this forever</i>

01:27.810 --> 01:33.940
<i>My changing feelings are driving me crazy</i>

01:33.940 --> 01:39.240
<i>The moment you turn to face me,
 take that! Telepathy</i>

01:39.240 --> 01:44.700
<i>If only we could feel the same thing</i>

01:44.700 --> 01:49.580
<i>I want to kick this pesky subtlety away</i>

01:49.580 --> 01:55.590
<i>I want to know everything, 
I want to know everything</i>

01:55.590 --> 01:58.130
<i>I can't fool you forever</i>

01:58.130 --> 02:00.760
<i>I can't keep this hidden</i>

02:00.760 --> 02:05.520
<i>I want to shout out my secret, AHHH</i>

02:07.430 --> 02:09.980
<i>Take that! Telepathy</i>

02:09.980 --> 02:12.440
<i>Te-te-te-telepathy</i>

02:13.150 --> 02:15.530
<i>Telepathy</i>

02:17.190 --> 02:20.990
<b>The Night of the Summer Festival</b>

02:17.990 --> 02:19.660
"The Night of the Summer Festival."

02:21.450 --> 02:25.450
D-Do you want to go see 
the fireworks with me?

02:25.450 --> 02:27.000
The fireworks?

02:28.410 --> 02:30.870
Are those two gonna be with us again?

02:30.870 --> 02:34.960
N-No! This time... just us two!

02:34.960 --> 02:36.670
It'll be just us two.

02:36.670 --> 02:38.340
Just us, huh?

02:39.090 --> 02:41.140
Okay. Let's go.

02:41.590 --> 02:45.100
<i>Huh? He doesn't seem that excited.</i>

02:45.100 --> 02:46.390
<i>Normally, he's like...</i>

02:46.390 --> 02:49.850
Man, I can't wait for the fireworks!

02:53.940 --> 02:56.570
Should we really just let 
things go on like this?

02:56.570 --> 02:57.650
Like what?

02:57.990 --> 03:00.240
The way Jun-kun and Tomo-chan are going,

03:00.240 --> 03:04.240
they could end up getting together 
like a normal guy and girl.

03:04.780 --> 03:07.830
I was just wondering, would that
 really be a good thing?

03:09.870 --> 03:11.540
Shut up.

03:13.920 --> 03:16.710
<i>Just me and Tomo seeing the fireworks, huh?</i>

03:17.500 --> 03:20.840
<i>I'm so happy. Like, more than I should be.</i>

03:21.300 --> 03:23.760
I love you, Jun!

03:25.260 --> 03:29.350
<i>Nah... She didn't mean 
it that way... I'm sure.</i>

03:30.310 --> 03:31.270
<i>Probably.</i>

03:35.440 --> 03:38.820
<i>I feel like Jun's been acting weird lately.</i>

03:39.400 --> 03:43.410
<i>When we went to the beach, 
he didn't seem all that into it.</i>

03:44.370 --> 03:47.620
<i>And just today... Could it be...</i>

03:47.870 --> 03:49.160
Summer exhaustion?

03:49.160 --> 03:51.330
It's not.

03:53.540 --> 03:57.040
<i>When Tomo came to me to 
tell me she loved Junichiro,</i>

03:57.540 --> 04:00.670
<i>I gave her a hackneyed response 
without even thinking about it.</i>

04:01.220 --> 04:04.010
Then why don't you try being more feminine?

04:04.510 --> 04:09.180
<i>And then Tomo dedicated herself to 
the idea way more than I expected.</i>

04:09.720 --> 04:13.640
<i>She even started showing interest 
in more girlish leisure activities.</i>

04:14.520 --> 04:18.860
<i>Maybe I really was wrong, like Carol said...</i>

04:20.150 --> 04:25.280
<i>About what I should have said to 
her back then as her best friend.</i>

04:26.990 --> 04:31.000
<i>But I have no intention of going back now.</i>

04:32.040 --> 04:38.710
<i>If I use him, Tomo and 
I can do more... more...</i>

04:46.050 --> 04:46.840
Huh?

04:47.850 --> 04:52.810
<b>The Day of the Fireworks Show</b>

04:49.810 --> 04:52.810
Jun, you're going to see the 
fireworks with Tomo-chan?

04:52.810 --> 04:53.890
Yeah.

04:54.560 --> 04:56.060
Good luck!

04:56.060 --> 04:56.900
Thanks.

04:58.020 --> 05:00.860
<i>I'm hyped, but also not.</i>

05:01.360 --> 05:03.900
<i>I'm happy, but also anxious.</i>

05:04.490 --> 05:08.490
<i>I'm gonna go figure out what 
this annoying feeling is.</i>

05:10.450 --> 05:14.160
Misuzu-chan, let's go watch the fireworks.

05:14.160 --> 05:15.370
No.

05:15.370 --> 05:18.920
Aw, c'mon. Ko-chan's coming, too.

05:18.920 --> 05:22.460
Senpai's going? Then wouldn't 
I be a third wheel?

05:22.460 --> 05:25.720
If it means you end up alone, I'm not going.

05:25.720 --> 05:26.430
Hmph.

05:26.970 --> 05:28.180
What's your deal?

05:34.180 --> 05:36.560
Sorry, Jun! Were you waiting long?

05:40.810 --> 05:44.440
Mom told me I should wear this...

05:45.280 --> 05:47.700
and it took a while to put it on.

05:50.700 --> 05:52.870
What's wrong? You okay?

05:52.870 --> 05:54.830
Sorry, I'm fi—

05:55.370 --> 05:58.420
Actually... maybe not quite.

05:58.420 --> 06:00.210
Are you feeling sick?

06:04.550 --> 06:05.800
<b>Goldfish Scooping</b>

06:08.130 --> 06:11.180
I'm back again this year, old fart.

06:11.430 --> 06:15.180
Hey, Jun-bo. Tomo-chan's 
not with you this year?

06:15.560 --> 06:18.390
Did you forget what I look like?

06:20.980 --> 06:23.440
What?! <i>You're</i> Tomo-chan?!

06:23.440 --> 06:25.230
Something wrong with that?

06:26.030 --> 06:29.450
I can't believe the stall-destroying 
demon of the summer festival

06:29.450 --> 06:32.120
grew up to be such a beauty.

06:32.620 --> 06:33.830
Gotta save this moment.

06:34.540 --> 06:39.750
Oh? Is that what you guys have 
been calling me behind my back?

06:42.840 --> 06:45.250
<i>Calling all vendors! They're back!</i>

06:45.250 --> 06:47.050
Tomo-chan and Jun-bo?!

06:48.380 --> 06:50.470
<i>Try not to die of shock when you see this!</i>

06:49.510 --> 06:50.220
On my way with provisions 




Roger! 




Tomo and Jun-bo are here

06:50.970 --> 06:53.300
Wh-What?!

06:53.300 --> 06:56.020
Th-This is that out-of-control tomboy?!

06:56.020 --> 06:58.980
She looks like a gravure idol in a yukata!

06:59.230 --> 07:01.520
I'll take one dish of ammo.

07:04.900 --> 07:06.230
<i>Yeah, but...</i>

07:06.690 --> 07:08.150
1st Prize

07:07.070 --> 07:09.610
<i>She's still the same on the inside!</i>

07:10.450 --> 07:12.910
I wish you'd said that sooner.

07:16.040 --> 07:18.790
That's my secret technique, the Triple Shot!

07:19.120 --> 07:22.250
You're holding hands so naturally.

07:22.250 --> 07:25.420
Yeah. If I let go of her hand...

07:26.500 --> 07:27.460
See?

07:30.380 --> 07:32.550
I can get her back pretty quickly, though.

07:32.550 --> 07:33.970
You've got it rough, huh?

07:34.930 --> 07:36.760
That looks like you, Ko-chan.

07:37.010 --> 07:38.100
What does?

07:39.140 --> 07:40.560
This is Ko-chan.

07:40.560 --> 07:42.020
Uh... it is?

07:42.480 --> 07:44.020
This is Tomo-chan.

07:44.020 --> 07:45.440
She'll get mad at you.

07:46.020 --> 07:47.190
Misuzu-chan.

07:47.190 --> 07:48.610
<i>I'll</i> get mad at you.

07:48.940 --> 07:50.650
Take whichever one you want.

07:55.280 --> 07:59.450
Hey, check it out, Jun! 
These handcrafted candies are incredible!

07:59.950 --> 08:00.700
Huh?

08:01.370 --> 08:03.920
Who's Jun? Your boyfriend?

08:04.250 --> 08:06.460
I-I don't have a boyfriend!

08:06.460 --> 08:07.880
Oh, so you're free, huh?

08:09.090 --> 08:11.380
Come hang out with us, then.

08:17.390 --> 08:19.430
What the hell?

08:19.430 --> 08:21.560
She <i>does</i> have a boyfriend.

08:24.850 --> 08:26.770
Uh... Jun...

08:27.270 --> 08:29.150
Thanks for helping me—

08:29.150 --> 08:30.230
Sorry.

08:30.230 --> 08:31.240
Huh?

08:32.240 --> 08:35.160
I'm sure you could've 
handled that by yourself.

08:36.660 --> 08:37.870
Jun...

08:37.870 --> 08:40.080
I butted in again.

08:40.080 --> 08:41.540
Would it...

08:41.540 --> 08:45.250
Would it kill you to let me thank you?!

08:45.960 --> 08:48.840
What the hell do you mean, 
I could've handled it myself?!

08:49.210 --> 08:52.550
I might be strong in a fight, but there 
are some things I just can't do!

08:52.550 --> 08:54.300
S-Sorry...

08:54.300 --> 08:58.100
Yeah, so... I'm gonna thank you now!

08:58.100 --> 08:59.050
Listen good!

08:59.300 --> 09:00.720
S-Sure.

09:02.810 --> 09:04.060
Thank you.

09:07.400 --> 09:11.320
I'm really glad you were there for me.

09:12.110 --> 09:13.150
Thanks.

09:24.830 --> 09:27.120
I think the fireworks are about to start.

09:27.120 --> 09:28.790
I know a great spot to watch from.

09:29.130 --> 09:31.050
O-Okay...

09:32.090 --> 09:34.800
<i>What... was that?</i>

09:41.720 --> 09:45.560
<i>Something's definitely off about him today.</i>

09:46.640 --> 09:51.190
<i>Is he... actually starting to notice me now?</i>

09:51.900 --> 09:53.190
<i>If he is...</i>

09:53.860 --> 09:57.400
<i>Maybe this time, I can get 
my feelings across for real.</i>

09:59.820 --> 10:02.330
Welp, I bought it.

10:02.740 --> 10:03.870
Do I look cute?

10:03.330 --> 10:05.830
<i>I'm even more of a 
third wheel than I thought.</i>

10:09.710 --> 10:10.790
Is that...

10:11.460 --> 10:13.550
I'm not letting you go anywhere.

10:13.800 --> 10:14.800
Let's go.

10:14.800 --> 10:17.930
<i>That's why she invited me along?</i>

10:17.930 --> 10:19.800
<i>This squishy bitch...</i>

10:23.510 --> 10:26.560
<i>If I'm gonna tell him, I should 
do it before the fireworks start.</i>

10:27.060 --> 10:28.440
<i>Now's my only chance.</i>

10:29.270 --> 10:30.190
Jun!

10:31.020 --> 10:32.730
L-Listen...

10:33.230 --> 10:34.020
What?

10:36.740 --> 10:39.910
<i>I feel like I can make him 
understand this time.</i>

10:40.450 --> 10:43.330
<i>And if that happens, 
what we have now will end.</i>

10:43.870 --> 10:47.290
<i>Our "now" will end, 
and "something" will begin.</i>

10:48.410 --> 10:49.420
What is it?

10:50.330 --> 10:52.670
<i>But what is "something"?</i>

10:53.460 --> 10:56.420
<i>It's not like there's even anything I want.</i>

10:59.470 --> 11:03.010
<i>I just wanted to make Jun my own.</i>

11:05.600 --> 11:06.810
<i>Now isn't the time.</i>

11:08.810 --> 11:11.940
<i>There's no chance for us right now.</i>

11:18.860 --> 11:20.280
They're pretty, huh?

11:20.650 --> 11:21.610
Yeah.

11:29.080 --> 11:30.540
That was a lot of fun!

11:30.540 --> 11:31.460
Yeah.

11:32.830 --> 11:38.010
<i>I still haven't figured out what 
this feeling I have for Tomo is.</i>

11:38.510 --> 11:39.550
Hey, Jun!

11:42.430 --> 11:43.890
Let's do this again!

11:45.970 --> 11:47.720
<i>But I did figure out one thing.</i>

11:48.640 --> 11:49.980
<i>I can't...</i>

11:51.100 --> 11:53.400
<i>have a real punching match 
with Tomo ever again.</i>

11:57.070 --> 12:00.990
<b>The Distance</b>

11:57.070 --> 12:00.990
<b>Between Them</b>

11:57.900 --> 11:59.610
"The Distance Between Them."

12:03.820 --> 12:05.780
What's wrong, Tomo-chan?

12:06.160 --> 12:09.160
You're starting the new term 
in unusually low spirits.

12:09.160 --> 12:10.790
Junichiro again?

12:10.790 --> 12:12.120
Yeah.

12:12.120 --> 12:17.040
I'm pretty sure Jun's starting 
to be careful around me.

12:17.040 --> 12:18.460
Isn't that good?

12:18.460 --> 12:21.920
No, the way he's doing it is just...

12:22.840 --> 12:25.220
Hey, Tomo. Mornin'.

12:27.300 --> 12:28.310
<i>His pinky?!</i>

12:29.810 --> 12:31.270
Let's go to school.

12:31.270 --> 12:33.440
Frankly, it's creepy!

12:33.440 --> 12:35.230
That's frank, all right.

12:38.900 --> 12:42.490
Is that how it's always 
gonna be from now on?

12:42.490 --> 12:44.740
What am I gonna do?

12:46.280 --> 12:49.450
Things with Tomo-chan and 
Jun-kun are starting to change.

12:49.830 --> 12:53.120
Just like you planned it, Misuzu-chan! Right?

12:53.450 --> 12:56.000
You don't seem very happy, though.

12:56.000 --> 12:57.420
Just shut up.

13:00.590 --> 13:03.720
<i>What is that squishy bitch trying to do?</i>

13:04.170 --> 13:06.720
<i>She doesn't seem like she wants 
to get in the way, but...</i>

13:07.010 --> 13:08.350
<i>And Tomo...</i>

13:08.350 --> 13:11.930
<i>She's gonna have to grow 
up one of these days.</i>

13:11.930 --> 13:13.890
<i>Same goes for Junichiro.</i>

13:14.440 --> 13:16.980
<i>So what's wrong with things changing now?</i>

13:18.480 --> 13:22.530
<i>To go from best friends with no 
reservations around each other to lovers...</i>

13:23.150 --> 13:25.610
<i>If that happens to those two...</i>

13:26.490 --> 13:27.660
<i>I'll...</i>

13:29.330 --> 13:32.450
Man, shit's been so dull for us lately.

13:32.700 --> 13:35.040
It's all because of that giant woman!

13:35.040 --> 13:37.460
We gotta get back at her somehow!

13:38.380 --> 13:39.790
That's...

13:40.920 --> 13:42.300
Not you!

13:50.850 --> 13:51.720
Yo.

13:51.720 --> 13:53.310
Got a sec?

13:53.680 --> 13:55.020
Don't touch me.

13:56.810 --> 13:59.440
What the hell is this weird intensity?!

13:59.440 --> 14:00.650
Hey!

14:02.400 --> 14:04.610
I know all of your faces now.

14:06.240 --> 14:09.370
Misuzu-chan, what're you doing?

14:09.370 --> 14:11.990
Is she another one of Aizawa's buddies?

14:13.040 --> 14:16.120
She has nothing to do with me or Tomo.

14:16.120 --> 14:17.750
She's just a classmate.

14:18.330 --> 14:20.460
Fine, then. Let's go.

14:21.130 --> 14:22.420
Wait!

14:22.420 --> 14:26.260
What? You want us to play with you, t—

14:33.680 --> 14:35.930
You okay?! Hang in there, man!

14:35.930 --> 14:36.680
Move, now!

14:43.690 --> 14:45.150
What are you doing?

14:46.530 --> 14:49.150
Where the hell did they go?!

14:53.620 --> 14:54.740
Over there!

15:01.750 --> 15:05.500
Well, what to do now?

15:07.460 --> 15:08.380
Yeah?

15:09.220 --> 15:10.760
<i>It's me.</i>

15:10.760 --> 15:12.180
Gundo?

15:12.180 --> 15:15.140
I don't remember giving you my number.

15:15.140 --> 15:17.640
<i>I'm in kind of a tight spot right now.</i>

15:17.640 --> 15:18.930
<i>Come help me.</i>

15:19.690 --> 15:22.060
I'm at the abandoned 
factory near the school.

15:22.060 --> 15:23.020
Carol's here, too.

15:23.900 --> 15:25.940
<i>And don't tell Tomo.</i>

15:26.940 --> 15:28.490
I won't.

15:28.780 --> 15:30.320
Hey, Jun!

15:30.320 --> 15:32.990
I'm gonna go ahead and leave. 
I've got stuff to do.

15:32.990 --> 15:33.950
What stuff?

15:35.030 --> 15:35.990
Hang on.

15:36.870 --> 15:40.080
Where are you going with that 
bloodthirsty look on your face?

15:41.040 --> 15:42.710
<i>Damn it.</i>

15:44.380 --> 15:46.130
Misuzu and Carol?!

15:46.130 --> 15:47.670
That's really bad!

15:47.670 --> 15:50.340
Yeah, but I can take care of it by myself.

15:50.340 --> 15:52.090
Screw that! I'm going, too!

15:52.510 --> 15:54.600
You think I'm that useless?

15:54.600 --> 15:57.810
You idiot! It's not because 
I don't have faith in you!

15:58.180 --> 16:00.480
Those two are my friends!

16:00.480 --> 16:04.440
I can't just let someone else go help 
them while I wait around in safety!

16:07.190 --> 16:11.990
<i>Oh, yeah. That's the kind of 
person my best friend is.</i>

16:13.200 --> 16:14.490
Carol?

16:19.040 --> 16:20.870
Are you angry?

16:20.870 --> 16:24.540
Just so you know, it's not my 
fault you fell on your face.

16:24.540 --> 16:25.670
Hmph.

16:25.920 --> 16:28.920
I don't talk to people 
I have nothing to do with.

16:28.920 --> 16:30.630
Oh, <i>that's</i> why.

16:30.960 --> 16:32.050
I just said that

16:32.800 --> 16:35.890
because I thought things would be 
even worse if you got involved, too.

16:36.350 --> 16:40.600
I mean, I do think of you as...

16:40.600 --> 16:42.810
something like a friend, after all.

16:44.310 --> 16:46.150
Misuzu-chan!

16:46.900 --> 16:49.570
I thought I might be able 
to pull it off that time.

16:49.570 --> 16:51.490
It's not gonna be that easy.

16:51.490 --> 16:52.650
Also, you're filthy.

16:52.650 --> 16:55.110
Found you.

16:56.070 --> 16:58.080
I've been dying to see you.

17:04.370 --> 17:06.210
Heya, Senpai.

17:07.040 --> 17:08.670
I've been dying to see you.

17:09.250 --> 17:11.880
Why don't we go somewhere 
else and have some fun?

17:15.090 --> 17:17.220
I guess Tomo-chan showed up after all.

17:17.220 --> 17:20.890
That's just who she is. 
I had a feeling she'd come.

17:20.890 --> 17:23.600
I love Tomo-chan for being like that.

17:24.310 --> 17:25.890
You don't, Misuzu-chan?

17:38.160 --> 17:39.530
Damn it, Jun!

17:39.830 --> 17:42.700
I told you, this is <i>my</i> fight!

17:43.830 --> 17:45.250
Yeah, yeah.

17:46.250 --> 17:48.460
<i>I'll leave this two the two of them</i>

17:48.460 --> 17:51.090
<i>and look for Carol and Gundo-san.</i>

17:51.840 --> 17:54.970
Come on, take those dirty 
clothes off already.

17:54.970 --> 17:56.340
But it's cold.

17:57.300 --> 17:58.430
There you are!

17:58.430 --> 17:59.600
Caro—

18:00.050 --> 18:01.310
Misaki-senpai?

18:01.310 --> 18:03.100
Oh, it really is Ko-chan!

18:08.850 --> 18:10.560
You're the only one left.

18:10.560 --> 18:13.280
It's about time you learned your lesson.

18:13.280 --> 18:14.400
Damn it!

18:16.860 --> 18:18.700
Hey, you punks.

18:19.070 --> 18:21.530
What did you do to Carol?!

18:23.040 --> 18:24.620
Was it you?

18:24.620 --> 18:27.870
Are you the one who did 
indecent things to Carol?

18:28.170 --> 18:30.380
Misaki-senpai? What's wrong?

18:30.380 --> 18:32.090
Wh-What are you talking about?!

18:32.090 --> 18:33.800
Don't you play dumb with me!

18:34.460 --> 18:38.800
She's such a sweet, pure girl, and you...

18:38.800 --> 18:40.550
And you...!

18:41.100 --> 18:45.220
Ko-chan got angry for my sake!

18:45.220 --> 18:48.810
Just correct the misunderstanding 
before someone dies.

18:49.560 --> 18:51.980
You were just changing clothes?

18:51.980 --> 18:53.570
Yep, that's right.

18:54.110 --> 18:57.740
How could I make such a stupid mistake?

18:58.200 --> 19:01.450
That made me happy, though. Thank you.

19:04.080 --> 19:06.160
Tomo, you can go on home.

19:06.540 --> 19:08.210
What are you gonna do?

19:08.710 --> 19:11.580
There's something I need 
to talk to him about.

19:12.330 --> 19:15.000
Don't worry. I'll be fine.

19:15.000 --> 19:17.050
Yeah? Okay, then.

19:17.050 --> 19:18.510
You sure about this?

19:18.510 --> 19:21.300
If Misuzu says she'll be fine, she'll be fine.

19:21.300 --> 19:22.340
Let's go.

19:26.310 --> 19:28.100
What do you wanna talk about?

19:28.100 --> 19:30.190
Want me to play with you?

19:30.190 --> 19:33.690
Look at you, acting tough the moment 
Tomo and Junichiro are gone.

19:33.690 --> 19:36.110
It's almost refreshing how weak you are.

19:36.110 --> 19:36.980
What?!

19:36.980 --> 19:38.320
But weak or not,

19:38.320 --> 19:42.280
even a petty thug like you must 
know about the Aizawa Dojo, right?

19:43.410 --> 19:47.120
All the bad guys around 
here know about that!

19:47.120 --> 19:50.250
The legendary delinquent leader, Aizawa Goro,

19:50.250 --> 19:52.540
and his band of wack jobs who 
want to change the world!

19:53.130 --> 19:55.840
Well, Tomo is his only daughter.

19:57.000 --> 20:00.340
P-Please forgive me! I had no idea!

20:00.340 --> 20:04.090
I heard you're gathering all the punks 
in this area to start up a team.

20:04.430 --> 20:08.640
If any of your buddies or wannabe 
gangsters mess with my friends again,

20:08.640 --> 20:12.730
I'll make sure you're the 
one who pays for it.

20:12.730 --> 20:14.810
It's not like I can control them all!

20:14.810 --> 20:16.480
Do you know how many there are?!

20:16.480 --> 20:18.280
Whether you can or not, you'd better.

20:18.280 --> 20:21.320
Devote your entire body and 
soul to protecting them.

20:21.320 --> 20:24.620
P-Protecting... who?

20:25.070 --> 20:28.580
My friends and me... and yourself.

20:36.790 --> 20:39.090
You're as ruthless as ever, I see.

20:40.170 --> 20:42.380
Oh, Junichiro. You're still here?

20:42.880 --> 20:45.680
You should've threatened them 
<i>before</i> they came after you.

20:45.680 --> 20:47.220
It didn't occur to me.

20:47.220 --> 20:48.100
Liar.

20:48.390 --> 20:51.270
You ran to this particular 
place on purpose, didn't you?

20:52.230 --> 20:56.480
He tried to mess with me and my friend.

20:56.480 --> 20:58.900
I wasn't going to let him 
walk away unscathed.

21:00.480 --> 21:01.610
You...

21:01.860 --> 21:03.860
are not gonna die a pleasant death.

21:03.860 --> 21:08.330
I never expected a pleasant
 death in the first place.

21:13.460 --> 21:15.710
Why did you bother waiting for me?

21:16.080 --> 21:18.420
Well, you <i>are</i> still a girl, you know.

21:19.710 --> 21:21.420
So is Tomo.

21:21.880 --> 21:23.880
Yeah, but...

21:23.880 --> 21:27.180
With her, it's not about 
being a guy or a girl.

21:29.720 --> 21:31.170
I don't want to hear it.

21:31.170 --> 21:34.280
Not from you or that squishy bitch.

21:34.280 --> 21:35.400
Squishy?

21:35.850 --> 21:37.810
<b>Aizawa</b>

21:35.860 --> 21:37.400
I'm heading out.

21:38.160 --> 21:41.200
<i>I really blew it yesterday.</i>

21:41.200 --> 21:44.660
<i>I lost my cool and acted 
like a savage again.</i>

21:45.250 --> 21:48.950
<i>And just when he was starting 
to notice me lately.</i>

21:49.310 --> 21:50.650
Morning, Tomo.

21:51.030 --> 21:52.100
Jun...

21:52.100 --> 21:54.450
What's wrong? Let's go to school.

21:57.370 --> 22:00.590
That's it, Jun! That's perfect!

22:00.590 --> 22:03.510
That's <i>perfect</i>!

22:04.380 --> 22:06.000
What are you talking about?

22:06.340 --> 22:09.440
That's <i>perfect</i>!

22:10.890 --> 22:14.640
<i>(This suspicious behavior is...)</i>

22:14.640 --> 22:18.940
<i>Hey, you know, I'm all mixed up</i>

22:18.940 --> 22:23.400
<i>It's too complicated, I'm freaking out</i>

22:23.400 --> 22:25.940
<i>I want to look cute to you</i>

22:23.730 --> 22:29.280
<i>(crazy, crazy, drive me crazy, and that's…)</i>

22:25.940 --> 22:28.570
<i>So I'm plotting, bargaining, 
sly, and stubborn</i>

22:29.280 --> 22:33.080
<i>Dizzying love</i>

22:34.240 --> 22:38.670
<i>Just tell him to look at you</i>

22:38.670 --> 22:43.630
<i>And watch him stiffen up even more, 
because you're both so awkward</i>

22:43.630 --> 22:47.510
<i>What? Even if we're alike in that way</i>

22:47.510 --> 22:52.100
<i>It doesn't make me happy, 'cause it
 means our love is going nowhere</i>

22:52.100 --> 23:00.980
<i>Cloudy heart, swirling emotions—
I sense rain coming</i>

23:00.980 --> 23:10.070
<i>So I partly open my umbrella, 
then sneakily scoot closer to you</i>

23:10.070 --> 23:14.030
<i>Please notice the curl of my 
eyelashes as I keep blinking</i>

23:14.030 --> 23:18.960
<i>And don't say I'm acting weird</i>

23:18.960 --> 23:22.920
<i>All this plotting and bargaining 
is my sly plan to look cute to you</i>

23:22.920 --> 23:27.970
<i>Try to solve the riddle of 
this soft, dizzying love</i>

23:25.840 --> 23:30.090
<i>(Buzzing, fidgeting)</i>

23:30.340 --> 23:34.890
<i>Listen, I might be a bit 
tangled in my own web now</i>

23:34.890 --> 23:38.930
<i>But once you unravel the mystery, 
you'll see pure lo-love</i>
